{
  "title": "Boss: the cryptic invoice",
  "summary": "Turn an unreadable invoice calculator into code that explains itself.",
  "minutes": 15,
  "kind": "boss",
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "The job",
      "body": [
        "You have inherited a billing script. It works, customers are paying, and nobody dares touch it. Your job across these steps: **keep every number identical** while making the code readable.",
        "",
        "Each step checks behaviour with tests, and checks the structure with rules about names, constants and nesting."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "mode": "fix",
      "title": "Name everything",
      "prompt": [
        "Rename and add constants, without changing results:",
        "",
        "- method `C` becomes `LineTotal`, parameters `q` and `p` become `quantity` and `unitPrice`",
        "- `0.1m` becomes `BulkDiscount`, `10` becomes `BulkQuantity`"
      ],
      "starter": [
        "decimal C(int q, decimal p)",
        "{",
        "    var t = q * p;",
        "    if (q >= 10) t = t - t * 0.1m;",
        "    return t;",
        "}"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "const int BulkQuantity = 10;",
        "const decimal BulkDiscount = 0.1m;",
        "",
        "decimal LineTotal(int quantity, decimal unitPrice)",
        "{",
        "    var total = quantity * unitPrice;",
        "    if (quantity >= BulkQuantity) total -= total * BulkDiscount;",
        "    return total;",
        "}"
      ],
      "template": [
        "{{CODE}}",
        "Dojo.Eq(\"3 at 2.00\", 6.00m, LineTotal(3, 2.00m));",
        "Dojo.Eq(\"10 at 1.00 gets the bulk discount\", 9.00m, LineTotal(10, 1.00m));",
        "Dojo.Eq(\"BulkQuantity\", 10, BulkQuantity);",
        "Dojo.Eq(\"BulkDiscount\", 0.1m, BulkDiscount);"
      ],
      "forbid": [
        {
          "pattern": "\\*\\s*0\\.1m",
          "message": "No bare 0.1"
        },
        {
          "pattern": ">=\\s*10\\b",
          "message": "No bare 10"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "mode": "fix",
      "title": "Guard and flatten",
      "prompt": [
        "`Status` decides what an invoice shows. Rewrite it with guard clauses and **no `else`**, same results, and name the 30 `DaysOverdueAfter`:",
        "",
        "- not sent: `draft`",
        "- paid: `paid`",
        "- more than 30 days since sending: `overdue`",
        "- otherwise `due`"
      ],
      "starter": [
        "string Status(bool sent, bool paid, int daysSinceSent)",
        "{",
        "    if (sent)",
        "    {",
        "        if (!paid)",
        "        {",
        "            if (daysSinceSent > 30) return \"overdue\";",
        "            else return \"due\";",
        "        }",
        "        else return \"paid\";",
        "    }",
        "    else return \"draft\";",
        "}"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "const int DaysOverdueAfter = 30;",
        "",
        "string Status(bool sent, bool paid, int daysSinceSent)",
        "{",
        "    if (!sent) return \"draft\";",
        "    if (paid) return \"paid\";",
        "    if (daysSinceSent > DaysOverdueAfter) return \"overdue\";",
        "    return \"due\";",
        "}"
      ],
      "template": [
        "{{CODE}}",
        "Dojo.Eq(\"draft\", \"draft\", Status(false, false, 99));",
        "Dojo.Eq(\"paid\", \"paid\", Status(true, true, 99));",
        "Dojo.Eq(\"overdue\", \"overdue\", Status(true, false, 31));",
        "Dojo.Eq(\"due at 30 days\", \"due\", Status(true, false, 30));",
        "Dojo.Eq(\"DaysOverdueAfter\", 30, DaysOverdueAfter);"
      ],
      "forbid": [
        {
          "pattern": "\\belse\\b",
          "message": "No else"
        },
        {
          "pattern": ">\\s*30\\b",
          "message": "No bare 30"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "mode": "fix",
      "title": "Split the monster",
      "prompt": [
        "`Invoice` builds a whole invoice in one block. Split it into small methods at one level of abstraction, keeping the text identical:",
        "",
        "- `decimal Subtotal(List<Line> lines)` sums `Qty * Price`",
        "- `decimal Tax(decimal subtotal)` is `subtotal * TaxRate` (`TaxRate` = `0.2m`), rounded to 2 decimals",
        "- `string FormatLine(Line line)` returns e.g. `2 x Pen @ 1.50`",
        "- `string Invoice(List<Line> lines)` uses them: the line strings, then `Subtotal: ...`, `Tax: ...`, `Total: ...`, one per line",
        "",
        "`Invoice` itself must not contain a `foreach`. `Line(string Name, int Qty, decimal Price)` is a record provided by the tests."
      ],
      "starter": [
        "string Invoice(List<Line> lines)",
        "{",
        "    var sb = new StringBuilder();",
        "    decimal s = 0;",
        "    foreach (var l in lines)",
        "    {",
        "        sb.AppendLine($\"{l.Qty} x {l.Name} @ {l.Price:F2}\");",
        "        s += l.Qty * l.Price;",
        "    }",
        "    var t = Math.Round(s * 0.2m, 2);",
        "    sb.AppendLine($\"Subtotal: {s:F2}\");",
        "    sb.AppendLine($\"Tax: {t:F2}\");",
        "    sb.Append($\"Total: {s + t:F2}\");",
        "    return sb.ToString();",
        "}"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "const decimal TaxRate = 0.2m;",
        "",
        "decimal Subtotal(List<Line> lines) => lines.Sum(l => l.Qty * l.Price);",
        "decimal Tax(decimal subtotal) => Math.Round(subtotal * TaxRate, 2);",
        "string FormatLine(Line line) => $\"{line.Qty} x {line.Name} @ {line.Price:F2}\";",
        "",
        "string Invoice(List<Line> lines)",
        "{",
        "    var subtotal = Subtotal(lines);",
        "    var tax = Tax(subtotal);",
        "    var body = lines.Select(FormatLine).ToList();",
        "    body.Add($\"Subtotal: {subtotal:F2}\");",
        "    body.Add($\"Tax: {tax:F2}\");",
        "    body.Add($\"Total: {subtotal + tax:F2}\");",
        "    return string.Join(Environment.NewLine, body);",
        "}"
      ],
      "template": [
        "{{CODE}}",
        "var dojoLines = new List<Line> { new(\"Pen\", 2, 1.50m), new(\"Pad\", 1, 4.25m) };",
        "Dojo.Eq(\"Subtotal\", 7.25m, Subtotal(dojoLines));",
        "Dojo.Eq(\"Tax\", 1.45m, Tax(7.25m));",
        "Dojo.Eq(\"FormatLine\", \"2 x Pen @ 1.50\", FormatLine(dojoLines[0]));",
        "Dojo.Eq(\"Invoice text is unchanged\",",
        "    string.Join(\"\\n\", \"2 x Pen @ 1.50\", \"1 x Pad @ 4.25\", \"Subtotal: 7.25\", \"Tax: 1.45\", \"Total: 8.70\"),",
        "    Invoice(dojoLines).Replace(\"\\r\\n\", \"\\n\"));",
        "record Line(string Name, int Qty, decimal Price);"
      ],
      "require": [
        {
          "pattern": "\\bTaxRate\\b",
          "message": "Uses TaxRate"
        },
        {
          "pattern": "\\bFormatLine\\b[\\s\\S]*\\bInvoice\\b[\\s\\S]*\\bFormatLine\\b",
          "message": "Invoice calls FormatLine"
        }
      ],
      "forbid": [
        {
          "pattern": "\\bforeach\\b",
          "message": "No foreach"
        }
      ],
      "hints": [
        "`string.Join(Environment.NewLine, ...)` over a list avoids a trailing newline.",
        "Build the list with `lines.Select(FormatLine).ToList()` and `Add` the three totals."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
